// POT API request examples

// Local URLs: use http://localhost:5242 for the non-Docker API, or http://localhost:5241 when
// running the Docker stack. The Development OpenAPI document is available at /openapi/v1.json.
// Health checks are anonymous and are useful for checking that the API is running:
//   GET /_health        - liveness
//   GET /_health/ready  - readiness, including the database

// Authentication:
// - The seven /api/auth requests below are AllowAnonymous: login, logout, refresh, password-reset
//   send/verify, and signup send/complete. All other /api routes require a valid bearer access
//   token; a fallback policy protects routes even if they do not declare a more specific policy.
// - This file uses Visual Studio's HTTP environment files, not VS Code REST Client variables.
//   Choose Development or Docker in the HTTP environment selector. Put personal credentials in
//   http-client.env.json.user beside http-client.env.json; the *.user pattern is ignored by Git.
//   Do not put real credentials in the shared http-client.env.json or commit them.
// - Send Login first. It returns an accessToken in the response body and sets the HTTP-only
//   pot_refresh_token cookie. The runner keeps that cookie in its own store and replays it on later
//   requests to the same host; a Cookie header written in this file is not sent, so Refresh and
//   Logout rely on Login and Refresh having run first in the same session.
// - Run Login before sending protected requests. The named login response supplies the bearer
//   accessToken to those requests, and the runner's cookie store supplies the refresh cookie. The
//   session-changing examples are last in this file because they end the session: Refresh rotates the
//   cookie and its refresh token is single-use, Logout revokes the session the presented token
//   belongs to (so later requests with that access token get 401), and Change password revokes every
//   session. Repeat Login before running them again.
// - Refresh and Logout need a cookie the runner can store and resend: it will not send a cookie
//   marked Secure over http, so select the Development environment (SecureOnly=false) for those two
//   requests. Configuration with Production settings, including the Docker stack, marks the cookie
//   Secure and those requests can only be exercised by a browser client.
// - Logout is AllowAnonymous at the route level, but also send the bearer token so the server can
//   identify the user, revoke the session, and clear the stored cookie. Only the current session is
//   revoked: another device keeps its access token, while the token issued for the revoked session
//   stops being accepted by /me.
// - Permission-protected operations additionally require the named permission. The API user needs:
//     account:view / account:manage       account reads / writes
//     expense:view / expense:manage       expense reads / writes
//     income:view / income:manage         income reads / writes
//     user:view / user:manage             user and role reads / user administration
//     site:view / site:manage             settings reads / site and settings writes
//     maintenance:export / maintenance:import
//     platform:manage                    approvals
//   Projections require account:view. Accrual status requires account:view, expense:view, and
//   income:view. Me endpoints require an authenticated user but no additional permission.
//   Updating a user requires authentication; editing another user also requires user:manage.
// - Fill in your values in http-client.env.json.user before sending; the placeholders in the shared
//   file are not real RowIds. Update requests that include Etag need the current Etag from the
//   corresponding GET response. Replace example dates, values, OTP codes and file paths with valid
//   data. The frequency, accrual-policy, renewal-mode, user-status, and approval-status values shown
//   below are the API's accepted enum names.
// - POST/PUT/DELETE/import requests can change or remove data. Review the request and target IDs
//   before sending; do not run destructive examples against data you need to keep.

// Endpoint coverage follows the current route registrations in Program.cs. The Scalar UI is a
// browser page rather than an HTTP operation, so it is not represented as a request here.

// Values come from the environment files, not from @ declarations:
//   http-client.env.json        checked in; shared values plus a placeholder for each personal value
//   http-client.env.json.user   ignored by Git; your own values, which override the shared file
// The values live there rather than in this file because other .http files use the same RowIds and
// because environment files are plain JSON with no comment support, so this list is their
// documentation. Keys:
//   ApiHost, ApiUrl     API host and the /api base of the selected environment (shared file)
//   Username, Password  an enabled, approved account to sign in with
//   AccountId           SELECT "RowId" FROM "Account"
//   ExpenseId           SELECT "RowId" FROM "Expense"
//   IncomeId            SELECT "RowId" FROM "Income"
//   UserId              SELECT "RowId" FROM "User" WHERE "Username" = 'your_username'
//   SiteId              SELECT "RowId" FROM "Site"
//   ApprovalUserId      SELECT "RowId" FROM "User" WHERE "Status" = 'Approval'
//   RoleId              SELECT "RowId" FROM "Role"
//   SettingKey          SELECT "Key" FROM "Setting" WHERE "Category" = 'EmailBudgetReminder'
// The settings requests use the EmailBudgetReminder category directly: it is an API enum name rather
// than a per-developer value.
// Note: keep every comment line non-empty. A comment line holding only the marker makes Visual Studio
// mis-read the next request, reporting HTTP0004 and HTTP0005 on its "### title" line and HTTP0006 on
// the request line, and that request loses its "Send request" link. Separate paragraphs with a blank
// line instead.

### Liveness health check (anonymous)
GET {{ApiHost}}/_health

### Readiness health check (anonymous)
GET {{ApiHost}}/_health/ready

### OpenAPI document (Development only; anonymous)
GET {{ApiHost}}/openapi/v1.json

### Login (anonymous; returns the access token and refresh cookie)
# @name login
POST {{ApiUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
User-Agent: POT Visual Studio HTTP file

{
  "username": "{{Username}}",
  "password": "{{Password}}"
}

### Get current user and permissions (authenticated)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/me/
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Request password-reset email (anonymous)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/auth/password-reset/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{Username}}"
}

### Verify password-reset code (anonymous)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/auth/password-reset/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{Username}}",
  "referenceCode": "replace-with-reference-code",
  "verificationCode": "replace-with-verification-code"
}

### Request signup verification (anonymous)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/auth/signup/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "new-user",
  "email": "new-user@example.com"
}

### Complete signup (anonymous)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/auth/signup/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "new-user",
  "referenceCode": "replace-with-reference-code",
  "verificationCode": "replace-with-verification-code"
}

### Get accounts (account:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get an account (account:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/accounts/{{AccountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create an account (account:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/accounts
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "HTTP example account",
  "balance": 1000,
  "reserved": 0
}

### Update an account (account:manage; use current Etag)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/accounts/{{AccountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "etag": 1,
  "description": "Updated HTTP example account",
  "balance": 1000,
  "reserved": 0
}

### Delete an account (account:manage; destructive)
DELETE {{ApiUrl}}/accounts/{{AccountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get expenses (expense:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get an expense (expense:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/expenses/{{ExpenseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create an expense (expense:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "HTTP example expense",
  "accrualStart": "2026-10-17",
  "nextDue": "2026-11-17",
  "endDate": null,
  "accrualPolicy": "Automatic",
  "frequency": "Months",
  "frequencyCount": 1,
  "amount": 100,
  "accountRowId": "{{AccountId}}",
  "note": "Example created from the REST Client file"
}

### Update an expense (expense:manage; use current Etag)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/expenses/{{ExpenseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "etag": 1,
  "excludeFromCalcs": false,
  "description": "Updated HTTP example expense",
  "accrualStart": "2026-10-17",
  "nextDue": "2026-11-17",
  "endDate": null,
  "accrualPolicy": "Automatic",
  "frequency": "Months",
  "frequencyCount": 1,
  "amount": 100,
  "accountRowId": "{{AccountId}}",
  "note": "Updated example"
}

### Renew expenses (expense:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/expenses/renew
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rowIds": ["{{ExpenseId}}"],
  "asOfDate": "2026-10-17",
  "mode": "Overdue"
}

### Toggle expense calculation exclusion (expense:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/expenses/toggleExclude
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rowIds": ["{{ExpenseId}}"]
}

### Delete an expense (expense:manage; destructive)
DELETE {{ApiUrl}}/expenses/{{ExpenseId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get incomes (income:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/incomes
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get an income (income:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/incomes/{{IncomeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create an income (income:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/incomes
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "HTTP example income",
  "nextDue": "2026-10-24",
  "endDate": null,
  "frequency": "Weeks",
  "frequencyCount": 1,
  "amount": 500,
  "accountRowId": "{{AccountId}}",
  "note": "Example created from the REST Client file"
}

### Update an income (income:manage; use current Etag)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/incomes/{{IncomeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "etag": 1,
  "excludeFromCalcs": false,
  "description": "Updated HTTP example income",
  "nextDue": "2026-10-24",
  "endDate": null,
  "frequency": "Weeks",
  "frequencyCount": 1,
  "amount": 500,
  "accountRowId": "{{AccountId}}",
  "note": "Updated example"
}

### Renew incomes (income:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/incomes/renew
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rowIds": ["{{IncomeId}}"],
  "asOfDate": "2026-10-17",
  "mode": "Overdue"
}

### Toggle income calculation exclusion (income:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/incomes/toggleExclude
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rowIds": ["{{IncomeId}}"]
}

### Delete an income (income:manage; destructive)
DELETE {{ApiUrl}}/incomes/{{IncomeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get users (user:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Update a user (authenticated; user:manage required when editing another user)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/users/{{UserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "etag": 1,
  "displayName": "Updated HTTP example user",
  "email": "user@example.com"
}

### Update user status (user:manage)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/users/{{UserId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "etag": 1,
  "status": "Enabled"
}

### Update user roles (user:manage)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/users/{{UserId}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "etag": 1,
  "roleIds": ["{{RoleId}}"]
}

### Invite a user (user:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/users/invite
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "invited-user",
  "email": "invited-user@example.com",
  "roleIds": ["{{RoleId}}"]
}

### Resend a user invitation (user:manage)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/users/{{UserId}}/resend-invite
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get roles (user:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Update site details (site:manage; use current Etag)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/sites/{{SiteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "etag": 1,
  "name": "Updated HTTP example site",
  "description": "Updated by the REST Client example"
}

### Get settings (site:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Create or update a setting (site:manage; use null Etag to create)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/settings/EmailBudgetReminder/{{SettingKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": "true",
  "etag": null
}

### Get financial projections (account:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/projections?startDate=2026-10-17&endDate=2027-10-17
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get accrual status (account:view, expense:view, income:view)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/accruals/status?AccountRowIds={{AccountId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Get pending approvals (platform:manage)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/approvals/pending
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Update a pending approval (platform:manage; use current Etag)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/approvals/{{ApprovalUserId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "etag": 1,
  "status": "Approved"
}

### Export data (maintenance:export)
GET {{ApiUrl}}/maintenance/export
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Import data from a ZIP file (maintenance:import; changes data)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/maintenance/import
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----PotRestClientBoundary

------PotRestClientBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="File"; filename="pot-export.zip"
Content-Type: application/zip

< ./path/to/pot-export.zip
------PotRestClientBoundary--

### Refresh access token (anonymous route; run Login immediately before this request)
# @name refresh
POST {{ApiUrl}}/auth/refresh

### Check the refreshed access token
GET {{ApiUrl}}/me/
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Logout after refresh (anonymous route; requires a successful Refresh immediately before this request)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Logout (anonymous route; ends the login session)
POST {{ApiUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Change current user's password (authenticated; revokes every session)
PUT {{ApiUrl}}/me/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "replace-with-current-password",
  "newPassword": "replace-with-new-password"
}
